{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjYEzM55ifVdzCmhHmXE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012k5wGveQzSHmPdAAWiDzwB","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The staff has four bars, read left to right.\n\nBar 1 is edition bar 17. It reads E4, then G3, then E4–F4 under a slur, then G3. The first note looks like an E4 written open. Its rhythm still fits bar 17's 8th, quarter, 8th, 8th, 8th.\n\nBar 2 is edition bar 18. It has the same figure: E4, G3, slurred E4–F4, G3.\n\nBar 3 is edition bar 19. It reads E4 and G3 beamed, then E4 and E4. Then comes a group of three notes with a \"+\" above it. That group is F4 8th and E4–F4 16ths. The copyist writes a \"+\" ornament where the edition has a grace G4.\n\nBar 4 is edition bar 20. It holds E4 quarter, then two quarter rests. A double bar with repeat dots follows. This matches bar 20, the last bar before the key change at bar 21.\n\nTwo things differ from the edition, and neither moves a bar boundary:\n- \"morendo\" sits under bar 1 here, but in bar 18 in the edition.\n- The dotted line ending in \"pianiss:\" above the staff continues a marking from the line before.","right":true,"insights":"This line was easy to match. Bars 17–18 repeat a clear figure, bar 20 is a lone note before the rests, and the double bar marks the end of the section. Two things made it slightly harder. The copyist's \"+\" stands where the edition has a grace note, and \"morendo\" sits a bar earlier than in the edition. An edition text that mentioned the double bar and repeat at bar 20 would have settled the end of the line at once."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5148,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5148},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo